-- ccc9-sexual-assault.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), ss 271 to 275 and s 278: sexual assault, with a weapon, aggravated; consent; belief in consent;
-- removal of a child from Canada; corroboration; recent complaint; spouse may be charged.
-- LAYER 1: the law as the text states it, from no one's point of view. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the
-- Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS: see ccc9-assault-officer.l4 (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled). MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the text says no in
-- its own words (an offence section's "who" condition and a failed "where" or "unless" gate, read as the text's no: NOTES.md, Marginal readings);
-- NOTHING where the text lists without closing the list, is silent, limits its own scope, or points outside the text.
-- SEAMS taken as inputs: `by s 265` / `by s 265(3)` (ccc8), `by s 2 <term>` (section 2), `by s 2.1` (restricted and prohibited firearm: s 84(1), ccc4),
-- `by s 2 criminal organization` (s 467.1(1)), `s 787(1)` (ccc29). "sexual assault" is not defined in the text: it is a fact the person states.

§ `Part VIII -- Sexual assault (s 271)`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 271
-- src:5063 | Sexual assault
-- src:5064 | 271 Everyone who commits a sexual assault is guilty of
@ref Criminal Code s 271 (src:5063-5064)
GIVEN `the accused commits a sexual assault` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 271 the accused is guilty of the offence of sexual assault` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the accused commits a sexual assault`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "sexual assault" is not defined in the text of section 271 or in section 2; the caller must state whether the act is one
    WHEN JUST x THEN IF x THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone who commits a sexual assault is guilty of"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 271(a); s 271(b)
-- src:5063 | Sexual assault
-- src:5064 | 271 Everyone who commits a sexual assault is guilty of
-- src:5065 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or, if the complainant is under the age of 16 years, to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:5066 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day or, if the complainant is under the age of 16 years, to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months.
@ref Criminal Code s 271 (src:5063-5066)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 271 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- "under the age of 16 years": a complainant of 15 years and 364 days is under 16; one of exactly 16 is not.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 271(a); s 271(b)
-- src:5065 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or, if the complainant is under the age of 16 years, to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:5066 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day or, if the complainant is under the age of 16 years, to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months.
@ref Criminal Code s 271(a), (b) (src:5065-5066)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `the complainant's age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 271 the punishment on the mode of proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN
        IF `the complainant's age in years` BELOW 16
        THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE)), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- (a): complainant under 16: not more than 14 years and a minimum of one year
        ELSE Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- (a): not more than 10 years
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN
        IF `the complainant's age in years` BELOW 16
        THEN Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`), (`imprisonment for a term of` `six months`), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- (b): complainant under 16: two years less a day and a minimum of six months
        ELSE Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- (b): not more than two years less a day

§ `Part VIII -- Sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm (s 272)`

-- src:5067 | Sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm
-- src:5068 | 272 (1) Every person commits an offence who, in committing a sexual assault,
@ref Criminal Code s 272(1) (src:5067-5068)
DECLARE `s 272(1) facts` HAS
    `the accused commits a sexual assault`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the accused carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon, by s 2 weapon`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the accused carries, uses or threatens to use an imitation of a weapon`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused threatens to cause bodily harm to a person other than the complainant`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused causes bodily harm to the complainant, by s 2 bodily harm`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the accused chokes, suffocates or strangles the complainant`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused is a party to the offence with any other person`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 272(1)(a)
-- src:5068 | 272 (1) Every person commits an offence who, in committing a sexual assault,
-- src:5069 | (a) carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon or an imitation of a weapon;
@ref Criminal Code s 272(1)(a) (src:5068-5069)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 272(1) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(1)(a) the accused, in committing a sexual assault, carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon or an imitation of a weapon` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST facts's `the accused commits a sexual assault`, `a weapon or an imitation of one`)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon or an imitation of a weapon"; NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "sexual assault" is not defined in the text, or s 2 weapon is itself not covered
    WHERE
        `a weapon or an imitation of one` MEANS
            `s 270 helper: at least one of these holds` (LIST facts's `the accused carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon, by s 2 weapon`, JUST (facts's `the accused carries, uses or threatens to use an imitation of a weapon`))

