§ `Part VIII -- Subsequent offences (ss 272(3), 272(4), 273(3), 273(4))`

-- An earlier conviction, as the text of subsection (3) asks about it: what the offence was, whether a firearm was used in committing it, the day the person was
-- convicted of it, and the days the person has spent in custody between that conviction and the conviction for the offence now being sentenced.
-- src:5082 | Subsequent offences
-- src:5083 | (3) In determining, for the purpose of paragraph (2)(a), whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:5084 | (a) an offence under this section;
-- src:5085 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244 or 244.2; or
-- src:5086 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1, 344 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
-- src:5087 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref Criminal Code s 272(3) (src:5082-5087)
DECLARE `s 272(3) earlier conviction` HAS
    `the offence`   IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `a firearm was used in the commission of the offence`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the person was convicted of the offence`   IS A DATE
    `the days spent in custody since that conviction`   IS A NUMBER

-- s 272(3)(a), (b), (c): which earlier offences are listed. Tested by section number (R1). "(c) ... if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence"
-- governs the whole of paragraph (c).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 272(3); s 272(3)(a); s 272(3)(b); s 272(3)(c)
-- src:5083 | (3) In determining, for the purpose of paragraph (2)(a), whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:5084 | (a) an offence under this section;
-- src:5085 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244 or 244.2; or
-- src:5086 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1, 344 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 272(3)(a) to (c) (src:5083-5086)
GIVEN conviction IS A `s 272(3) earlier conviction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 272(3) the earlier offence is one of those listed` MEANS
        conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 272
     OR (conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 85 AND (conviction's `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR conviction's `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
     OR conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 244
     OR conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 244.2
     OR (conviction's `a firearm was used in the commission of the offence`
         AND (   conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 220
              OR conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 236
              OR conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 239
              OR conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 273
              OR (conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 279 AND conviction's `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
              OR conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 279.1
              OR conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 344
              OR conviction's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 346))

-- s 272(4): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or
-- whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction." So the only dates asked are the two conviction dates; no commission date is an input.
-- Two convictions on the same day: the text does not say which is earlier (NOTHING-kind (silent)).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 272(4)
-- src:5088 | Sequence of convictions only
-- src:5089 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 272(4) (src:5088-5089)
GIVEN `the day the person was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE
      `the day the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(4) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day the person was convicted of the earlier offence` BELOW `the day the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the day the person was convicted of the earlier offence` ABOVE `the day the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say which of two convictions on the same day is earlier

-- s 272(3), closing words: "an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the
-- earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody."
-- Ten calendar years from the earlier conviction (`add years`), the days in custody not counted: ten years have elapsed when the later conviction, less the custody days,
-- is on or after the tenth anniversary of the earlier one. (Fork F-custody in NOTES.md: custody is taken as a count of days.)
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 272(3) closing words
-- src:5087 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref Criminal Code s 272(3), closing words (src:5087-5087)
GIVEN `the day the person was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE
      `the day the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
      `the days spent in custody in that time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 272(3) ten years have elapsed, not taking into account any time in custody` MEANS
    `add years` `the day the person was convicted of the earlier offence` 10 AT MOST (`the day the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` MINUS `the days spent in custody in that time`)

-- The whole of subsection (3) for one earlier conviction: is it to be considered an earlier offence?
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 272(3)
-- src:5082 | Subsequent offences
-- src:5083 | (3) In determining, for the purpose of paragraph (2)(a), whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:5084 | (a) an offence under this section;
-- src:5085 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244 or 244.2; or
-- src:5086 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1, 344 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
-- src:5087 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref Criminal Code s 272(3) (src:5082-5087)
GIVEN conviction IS A `s 272(3) earlier conviction`
      `the day the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(3) the earlier conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 272(3) the earlier offence is one of those listed` conviction) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence"
        IF `s 272(3) ten years have elapsed, not taking into account any time in custody` (conviction's `the day the person was convicted of the offence`) `the day the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` (conviction's `the days spent in custody since that conviction`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed"
        OTHERWISE `s 272(4) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` (conviction's `the day the person was convicted of the offence`) `the day the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`

§ `Part VIII -- Sexual assault with a weapon: punishment (s 272(2))`

-- s 272(2): the punishment depends on four limbs, and the limbs can overlap. (a.2) ("if the complainant is under the age of 16 years") is not limited to "any other case",
-- so a case with a firearm and a complainant under 16 is within (a) or (a.1) AND within (a.2), and the text does not say how the two limbs combine: fork F1 in NOTES.md.
-- This part answers (i) which limbs apply, (ii) the punishment under each limb as the text states it, and (iii) the one punishment only where exactly one limb applies.
-- src:5074 | Punishment
-- src:5075 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:5076 | (a) if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if any firearm is used in the commission of the offence and the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:5077 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
-- src:5078 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years;
-- src:5079 | (a.1) in any other case where a firearm is used in the commission of the offence, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of four years; and
-- src:5080 | (a.2) if the complainant is under the age of 16 years, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of five years; and
-- src:5081 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 272(2) (src:5074-5081)
DECLARE `s 272(2) limb` IS ONE OF
    `s 272(2)(a) a restricted or prohibited firearm, or a firearm for a criminal organization: first offence`
    `s 272(2)(a) a restricted or prohibited firearm, or a firearm for a criminal organization: second or subsequent offence`
    `s 272(2)(a.1) any other case where a firearm is used`
    `s 272(2)(a.2) the complainant is under the age of 16 years`
    `s 272(2)(b) any other case`

-- The facts the limbs of subsection (2) turn on (the same facts serve s 273(2), whose limbs have the same words).
-- src:5075 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:5076 | (a) if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if any firearm is used in the commission of the offence and the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:5077 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
-- src:5078 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years;
-- src:5079 | (a.1) in any other case where a firearm is used in the commission of the offence, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of four years; and
-- src:5080 | (a.2) if the complainant is under the age of 16 years, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of five years; and
-- src:5081 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 272(2) (src:5075-5081)
DECLARE `s 272(2) facts` HAS
    `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 restricted firearm`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 prohibited firearm`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2 firearm`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the offence is a second or subsequent offence, by subsection (3)`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the complainant's age in years`   IS A NUMBER

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 272(2)(a)
-- src:5076 | (a) if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if any firearm is used in the commission of the offence and the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:5077 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
-- src:5078 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years;
@ref Criminal Code s 272(2)(a) (src:5076-5078)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 272(2) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(2)(a) a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used, or a firearm is used for a criminal organization` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: at least one of these holds` (LIST facts's `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 restricted firearm`, facts's `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 prohibited firearm`, `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST facts's `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2 firearm`, facts's `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization`))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if any firearm is used in the commission of the offence and the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 84(1) (via s 2.1), s 2 firearm or s 467.1(1) is itself not covered

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 272(2)(a.1)
-- src:5079 | (a.1) in any other case where a firearm is used in the commission of the offence, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of four years; and
@ref Criminal Code s 272(2)(a.1) (src:5079-5079)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 272(2) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(2)(a.1) any other case where a firearm is used` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST facts's `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2 firearm`, `s 270 helper: the opposite of` (`s 272(2)(a) a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used, or a firearm is used for a criminal organization` facts))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other case where a firearm is used in the commission of the offence"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 2 firearm, s 84(1) or s 467.1(1) is itself not covered

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 272(2)(a.2)
