§ `Part VIII -- Meaning of consent, and when no consent is obtained (s 273.1)`

-- s 273.1(2): "no consent is obtained if" any of (a) to (e). Subsection (3) says the list does not limit the circumstances, so when none of (a) to (e) holds the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:5114 | No consent obtained
-- src:5115 | (2) For the purpose of subsection (1), no consent is obtained if
-- src:5116 | (a) the agreement is expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant;
-- src:5117 | (a.1) the complainant is unconscious;
-- src:5118 | (b) the complainant is incapable of consenting to the activity for any reason other than the one referred to in paragraph (a.1);
-- src:5119 | (c) the accused induces the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority;
-- src:5120 | (d) the complainant expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity; or
-- src:5121 | (e) the complainant, having consented to engage in sexual activity, expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue to engage in the activity.
@ref Criminal Code s 273.1(2) (src:5114-5121)
DECLARE `s 273.1(2) facts` HAS
    `the agreement is expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the complainant is unconscious`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the complainant is incapable of consenting to the activity for any reason other than unconsciousness`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused induces the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the complainant expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the complainant, having consented to engage in sexual activity, expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue to engage in the activity`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 273.1(3)
-- src:5122 | Subsection (2) not limiting
-- src:5123 | (3) Nothing in subsection (2) shall be construed as limiting the circumstances in which no consent is obtained.
@ref Criminal Code s 273.1(3) (src:5122-5123)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273.1(3) subsection (2) is a limit on the circumstances in which no consent is obtained` MEANS
    JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsection (2) shall be construed as limiting the circumstances in which no consent is obtained"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 273.1(2); s 273.1(2)(a); s 273.1(2)(a.1); s 273.1(2)(b); s 273.1(2)(c); s 273.1(2)(d); s 273.1(2)(e)
-- src:5114 | No consent obtained
-- src:5115 | (2) For the purpose of subsection (1), no consent is obtained if
-- src:5116 | (a) the agreement is expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant;
-- src:5117 | (a.1) the complainant is unconscious;
-- src:5118 | (b) the complainant is incapable of consenting to the activity for any reason other than the one referred to in paragraph (a.1);
-- src:5119 | (c) the accused induces the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority;
-- src:5120 | (d) the complainant expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity; or
-- src:5121 | (e) the complainant, having consented to engage in sexual activity, expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue to engage in the activity.
@ref Criminal Code s 273.1(2) (src:5114-5121)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 273.1(2) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273.1(2) no consent is obtained` MEANS
    IF     facts's `the agreement is expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant`
        OR facts's `the complainant is unconscious`
        OR facts's `the complainant is incapable of consenting to the activity for any reason other than unconsciousness`
        OR facts's `the accused induces the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority`
        OR facts's `the complainant expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity`
        OR facts's `the complainant, having consented to engage in sexual activity, expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue to engage in the activity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Nothing in subsection (2) shall be construed as limiting the circumstances in which no consent is obtained"

-- s 273.1(1): "Subject to subsection (2) and subsection 265(3), consent means ... the voluntary agreement of the complainant to engage in the sexual activity in question."
-- Where subsection (2) or s 265(3) says no consent is obtained, there is no consent; otherwise consent is the voluntary agreement.
