        IF `no consent is obtained under subsection (2), by s 273.1(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (2)": no consent is obtained in a circumstance listed in subsection (2)
        IF `no consent is obtained under subsection 265(3), by s 265(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (2) and subsection 265(3)"
        IF NOT `the complainant voluntarily agrees to engage in the sexual activity in question` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "consent means, for the purposes of sections 271, 272 and 273, the voluntary agreement of the complainant to engage in the sexual activity in question"
        IF `no consent is obtained under subsection 265(3), by s 265(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE   -- COMPARISON only (the result is JUST TRUE): subsection (2) is not JUST TRUE here (the branch above): it is a list that does not close (subsection (3)), so its NOTHING says only that none of its circumstances was shown, and the voluntary agreement stands (fork F in NOTES.md)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 265(3), in another part, is itself not covered

