§ `Part VIII -- Where belief in consent is not a defence (s 273.2)`

-- src:5124 | Where belief in consent not a defence
-- src:5125 | 273.2 It is not a defence to a charge under section 271, 272 or 273 that the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge, where
-- src:5126 | (a) the accused’s belief arose from
-- src:5127 | (i) the accused’s self-induced intoxication,
-- src:5128 | (ii) the accused’s recklessness or wilful blindness, or
-- src:5129 | (iii) any circumstance referred to in subsection 265(3) or 273.1(2) or (3) in which no consent is obtained;
-- src:5130 | (b) the accused did not take reasonable steps, in the circumstances known to the accused at the time, to ascertain that the complainant was consenting; or
-- src:5131 | (c) there is no evidence that the complainant’s voluntary agreement to the activity was affirmatively expressed by words or actively expressed by conduct.
@ref Criminal Code s 273.2 (src:5124-5131)
DECLARE `s 273.2 facts` HAS
    `the charge`   IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `the accused says the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the belief arose from the accused's self-induced intoxication`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the belief arose from the accused's recklessness or wilful blindness`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the belief arose from a circumstance in which no consent is obtained under subsection 265(3) or 273.1(2) or (3)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused did not take reasonable steps, in the circumstances known to the accused at the time, to ascertain that the complainant was consenting`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is no evidence that the complainant's voluntary agreement was affirmatively expressed by words or actively expressed by conduct`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 273.2
-- src:5124 | Where belief in consent not a defence
-- src:5125 | 273.2 It is not a defence to a charge under section 271, 272 or 273 that the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge, where
@ref Criminal Code s 273.2 (src:5124-5125)
GIVEN charge IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 273.2 the charge is under section 271, 272 or 273` MEANS
    charge's `section` EQUALS 271 OR charge's `section` EQUALS 272 OR charge's `section` EQUALS 273

-- The bar: "It is not a defence ... that the accused believed that the complainant consented ... where (a), (b) or (c)." JUST TRUE: the belief is barred as a defence.
-- JUST FALSE: none of (a), (b), (c): this section gives no bar on these facts (and nothing is said about whether the belief is then a defence). NOTHING: the charge is not under
-- section 271, 272 or 273, or no belief in consent is put forward: the bar is limited to those.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 273.2; s 273.2(a); s 273.2(a)(i); s 273.2(a)(ii); s 273.2(a)(iii); s 273.2(b); s 273.2(c)
-- src:5124 | Where belief in consent not a defence
-- src:5125 | 273.2 It is not a defence to a charge under section 271, 272 or 273 that the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge, where
-- src:5126 | (a) the accused’s belief arose from
-- src:5127 | (i) the accused’s self-induced intoxication,
-- src:5128 | (ii) the accused’s recklessness or wilful blindness, or
-- src:5129 | (iii) any circumstance referred to in subsection 265(3) or 273.1(2) or (3) in which no consent is obtained;
-- src:5130 | (b) the accused did not take reasonable steps, in the circumstances known to the accused at the time, to ascertain that the complainant was consenting; or
-- src:5131 | (c) there is no evidence that the complainant’s voluntary agreement to the activity was affirmatively expressed by words or actively expressed by conduct.
@ref Criminal Code s 273.2 (src:5124-5131)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 273.2 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273.2 the accused's belief in consent is not a defence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 273.2 the charge is under section 271, 272 or 273` (facts's `the charge`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a charge under section 271, 272 or 273"
        IF NOT facts's `the accused says the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge"
        IF     facts's `the belief arose from the accused's self-induced intoxication`
            OR facts's `the belief arose from the accused's recklessness or wilful blindness`
            OR facts's `the belief arose from a circumstance in which no consent is obtained under subsection 265(3) or 273.1(2) or (3)`
            OR facts's `the accused did not take reasonable steps, in the circumstances known to the accused at the time, to ascertain that the complainant was consenting`
            OR facts's `there is no evidence that the complainant's voluntary agreement was affirmatively expressed by words or actively expressed by conduct`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where"

§ `Part VIII -- Removal of a child from Canada (s 273.3)`

-- The person removed is described by age and residence; the intended act by the section it would offend if committed in Canada (R1: tested by section number).
-- src:5132 | Removal of child from Canada
-- src:5133 | 273.3 (1) No person shall do anything for the purpose of removing from Canada a person who is ordinarily resident in Canada and who is
-- src:5134 | (a) under the age of 16 years, with the intention that an act be committed outside Canada that if it were committed in Canada would be an offence against section 151 or 152 or subsection 160(3) or 173(2) in respect of that person;
-- src:5135 | (b) 16 years of age or more but under the age of eighteen years, with the intention that an act be committed outside Canada that if it were committed in Canada would be an offence against section 153 in respect of that person;
-- src:5136 | (c) under the age of 18 years, with the intention that an act be committed outside Canada that if it were committed in Canada would be an offence against section 155, subsection 160(2) or section 170, 171, 267, 268, 269, 271, 272, 273 or 320.102 in respect of that person; or
-- src:5137 | (d) under the age of 18 years, with the intention that an act be committed outside Canada that, if it were committed in Canada, would be an offence against section 293.1 in respect of that person or under the age of 16 years, with the intention that an act be committed outside Canada that, if it were committed in Canada, would be an offence against section 293.2 in respect of that person.
@ref Criminal Code s 273.3(1) (src:5132-5137)
DECLARE `s 273.3(1) facts` HAS
    `the accused does something for the purpose of removing the person from Canada`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is ordinarily resident in Canada`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's age in years`   IS A NUMBER
    `the accused intends that an act be committed outside Canada`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act, if committed in Canada, would be an offence in respect of that person against`   IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `the act, if committed in Canada, would be an offence`   IS A BOOLEAN

