    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb (b) states no penalty: the answer of s 787(1), taken as an input

§ `Part VIII -- Corroboration, recent complaint, and spouses (ss 274, 275, 278)`

-- s 274: the offences are named by section number (R1). Any subsection of a named section is within it.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 274
-- src:5142 | Corroboration not required
-- src:5143 | 274 If an accused is charged with an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160, 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272, 273, 286.1, 286.2 or 286.3, no corroboration is required for a conviction and the judge shall not instruct the jury that it is unsafe to find the accused guilty in the absence of corroboration.
