    IF `s 274 the charge is one of the offences named` charge
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an accused is charged with an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160, 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272, 273, 286.1, 286.2 or 286.3"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 274
-- src:5142 | Corroboration not required
-- src:5143 | 274 If an accused is charged with an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160, 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272, 273, 286.1, 286.2 or 286.3, no corroboration is required for a conviction and the judge shall not instruct the jury that it is unsafe to find the accused guilty in the absence of corroboration.
@ref Criminal Code s 274 (src:5142-5143)
GIVEN charge IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 274 the judge shall not instruct the jury that it is unsafe to find the accused guilty in the absence of corroboration` MEANS
    IF `s 274 the charge is one of the offences named` charge
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an accused is charged with an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160, 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272, 273, 286.1, 286.2 or 286.3"

-- s 275: sections 151, 152, 153, 153.1 and 155, subsections 160(2) and (3) and sections 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 and 273: section 160 only for subsections (2) and (3).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 275
-- src:5144 | Rules respecting recent complaint abrogated
-- src:5145 | 275 The rules relating to evidence of recent complaint are hereby abrogated with respect to offences under sections 151, 152, 153, 153.1 and 155, subsections 160(2) and (3) and sections 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 and 273.
@ref Criminal Code s 275 (src:5144-5145)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275 the rules relating to evidence of recent complaint are abrogated for the offence` MEANS
    IF     offence's `section` EQUALS 151 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 152 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 153 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 153.1 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 155
        OR (offence's `section` EQUALS 160 AND (offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(3)"))
        OR offence's `section` EQUALS 170 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 171 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 172 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 173
        OR offence's `section` EQUALS 271 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 272 OR offence's `section` EQUALS 273
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with respect to offences under sections 151, 152, 153, 153.1 and 155, subsections 160(2) and (3) and sections 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272 and 273"

-- s 278: "A husband or wife may be charged with an offence under section 271, 272 or 273 in respect of his or her spouse, whether or not the spouses were living together."
-- Whether the spouses were living together makes no difference: it is not an input. A charge under another section, or in respect of someone who is not the spouse, is outside the section.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278
-- src:5296 | Spouse May Be Charged
-- src:5297 | Spouse may be charged
-- src:5298 | 278 A husband or wife may be charged with an offence under section 271, 272 or 273 in respect of his or her spouse, whether or not the spouses were living together at the time the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge occurred.
@ref Criminal Code s 278 (src:5296-5298)
GIVEN charge IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the complainant is the accused's husband or wife` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278 a husband or wife may be charged with the offence in respect of his or her spouse` MEANS
    IF `s 273.2 the charge is under section 271, 272 or 273` charge AND `the complainant is the accused's husband or wife`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with an offence under section 271, 272 or 273 in respect of his or her spouse"


§ `Part VIII -- The prohibitions as regulative rules (ss 273.3(1), 274)`

-- The accused is the person in the seat; "No person shall" binds every person, and the core's Party has no `a person` constructor (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- The prohibition has no time limit and no consequence stated other than that the person is guilty of the offence of subsection (2): the rule carries no WITHIN.
DECLARE `s 273.3 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 273.3(1) do anything for the purpose of removing the person from Canada with the intention that the act be committed outside Canada`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 273.3(1)
-- src:5132 | Removal of child from Canada
-- src:5133 | 273.3 (1) No person shall do anything for the purpose of removing from Canada a person who is ordinarily resident in Canada and who is
-- src:5134 | (a) under the age of 16 years, with the intention that an act be committed outside Canada that if it were committed in Canada would be an offence against section 151 or 152 or subsection 160(3) or 173(2) in respect of that person;
-- src:5135 | (b) 16 years of age or more but under the age of eighteen years, with the intention that an act be committed outside Canada that if it were committed in Canada would be an offence against section 153 in respect of that person;
-- src:5136 | (c) under the age of 18 years, with the intention that an act be committed outside Canada that if it were committed in Canada would be an offence against section 155, subsection 160(2) or section 170, 171, 267, 268, 269, 271, 272, 273 or 320.102 in respect of that person; or
-- src:5137 | (d) under the age of 18 years, with the intention that an act be committed outside Canada that, if it were committed in Canada, would be an offence against section 293.1 in respect of that person or under the age of 16 years, with the intention that an act be committed outside Canada that, if it were committed in Canada, would be an offence against section 293.2 in respect of that person.
@ref Criminal Code s 273.3(1) (src:5132-5137)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 273.3(1) facts`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 273.3 act`
`s 273.3(1) the prohibition on removing a person from Canada` MEANS
    IF `s 273.3(1) the person and the intended act are within paragraphs (a) to (d)` facts
    THEN PARTY `the accused`
         SHANT `s 273.3(1) do anything for the purpose of removing the person from Canada with the intention that the act be committed outside Canada`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 273.3(1): something was done for the purpose of removing the person from Canada"
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no prohibition arises on these facts: this is not a finding that the act is allowed (the decision function answers NOTHING there)

DECLARE `s 274 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 274 instruct the jury that it is unsafe to find the accused guilty in the absence of corroboration`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 274
-- src:5142 | Corroboration not required
-- src:5143 | 274 If an accused is charged with an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160, 170, 171, 172, 173, 271, 272, 273, 286.1, 286.2 or 286.3, no corroboration is required for a conviction and the judge shall not instruct the jury that it is unsafe to find the accused guilty in the absence of corroboration.
@ref Criminal Code s 274 (src:5142-5143)
GIVEN charge IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 274 act`
`s 274 the judge's prohibition on a corroboration instruction` MEANS
    IF `s 274 the charge is one of the offences named` charge
    THEN PARTY `a judge`
         SHANT `s 274 instruct the jury that it is unsafe to find the accused guilty in the absence of corroboration`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "s 274: the jury was instructed that it is unsafe to find the accused guilty in the absence of corroboration"
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no prohibition arises on these facts: this is not a finding that the instruction may be given
